## 2. MANDATORY TECHNOLOGIES AND TOOLS

Use the following technologies exactly as required:

1. React.js — Build reusable, component-based user interfaces.
2. Vite — Set up the project and development server.
3. Tailwind CSS — Handle all styling, layouts, spacing, colors, typography, and responsiveness.
4. React Router DOM — Implement navigation and all required routes.
5. Lucide React — Provide consistent icons throughout the website.
6. React Hooks — Use useState and useEffect for application state and side effects.
7. Custom useLocalStorage Hook — Save and retrieve enrollment and progress information.
8. JavaScript — Store course, lesson, and instructor data in local files.
9. Git and GitHub — Manage source code and version history.
10. Vercel — Deploy the completed website.

### Allowed packages

Only use these additional packages:

* react-router-dom
* lucide-react
* tailwindcss
* @tailwindcss/vite

Use the standard React and Vite dependencies as well.

Do not install Redux, Bootstrap, Material UI, animation libraries, video-player libraries, form libraries, or additional state-management libraries.

Do not use TypeScript. Create the project using the React JavaScript template.

