## 13. ROUTING AND APPLICATION ARCHITECTURE

Implement routing with React Router DOM.

Wrap the application in BrowserRouter in main.jsx.

Create the following routes:

* / → Home
* /courses → Courses
* /courses/:courseId → CourseDetails
* /dashboard → Dashboard
* /learn/:courseId/:lessonId → Lesson
* * → NotFound

Render the shared Navbar and Footer through the main application layout.

Use:

* Link and NavLink for navigation.
* useNavigate for programmatic navigation.
* useParams to read courseId and lessonId.
* useSearchParams to initialize and manage course search and filters.

Unknown URLs must display a friendly Not Found page.

Unknown course and lesson IDs must also be handled safely.

Ensure direct URL navigation and browser refresh work correctly after deployment.

Do not use document.getElementById, querySelector, or innerHTML to manipulate the UI.

Use React state, props, event handlers, and conditional rendering.

Render lists with .map() and unique keys.

